SUMMARY:Run 6 mi: 10K-pace intervals
DESCRIPTION:10K: 1.5 WU\, 3x1 mi @ 10K pace\, 2' jog\, 1 CD\nPurpose of wee
 k: 10K build\, race-pace week: first 3x1 mile at goal pace (about 8:00) to
  learn the effort\, plus a longer sub-threshold session.\nPhase: Recover f
 rom the NYC Marathon DNF and\, on your doctor's advice\, ramp up very slow
 ly through December\, with long runs capped at 9 miles until 2027. Weeks 3
 -6 are a focused 10K build (threshold\, sub-threshold and race-pace work) 
 for the Boca 10K on Dec 27. Reassess in January.\nPace: Reps at 10K pace ~
 8:00/mi (not faster)\; WU/CD easy 9:40-10:30\nShoe: Mach 7\nWeek 4\, 1 Rec
 overy & slow ramp\, 20 mi total\nNote: 10K build\, race-pace week: first p
 ractice at goal pace. Hold 8:00\, not faster. Sub-threshold Thursday stays
  controlled (HR 160 or lower).
END:VEVENT
